<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="SK.PatchOperationReplaceExtended">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Bow_Short"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<label>Flat Bow</label>
			<description>This is the simplest bow which can be made with primitive tech and unrefined wood. Bows require a lot of training to use effectively, although this is the easiest type to use despite having a long draw time.</description>
			<graphicData>
				<texPath>Things/Weapons/VileBows/FlatBow</texPath>
				<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			</graphicData>
			<statBases Merge="True">
				<SightsEfficiency>0.95</SightsEfficiency>
				<ShotSpread>0.7</ShotSpread>
				<SwayFactor>1.5</SwayFactor>
				<Mass>1.2</Mass>
				<RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.2</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
			</statBases>
			<verbs>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.VerbPropertiesCE">
					<verbClass>CombatExtended.Verb_ShootCE</verbClass>
					<hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
					<defaultProjectile>Projectile_Arrow_Stone</defaultProjectile>
					<warmupTime>1.4</warmupTime>
					<range>35</range>
					<soundCast>Bow_Small</soundCast>
				</li>
			</verbs>
		</value>
	</Operation>


	<Operation Class="SK.PatchOperationReplaceExtended">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Bow_Great"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<label>Long Bow</label>
			<description>Your classic medieval bow shaped like a “D”. It can be mass-produced, and fires quite far (farther than a crossbow). Bows require a lot of training to use: An amateur archer may only be effective against targets within 10 or so meters, but a master can hit things 30 or so meters away.</description>
			<graphicData>
				<texPath>Things/Weapons/VileBows/Longbow</texPath>
				<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			</graphicData>
			<stuffCategories>
				<li>Woody</li>
			</stuffCategories>
			<costStuffCount>55</costStuffCount>
			<statBases Merge="True">
				<ShotSpread>0.5</ShotSpread>
				<SwayFactor>2.3</SwayFactor>
				<Mass>2.00</Mass>
				<RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.2</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
			</statBases>
			<verbs>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.VerbPropertiesCE">
					<verbClass>CombatExtended.Verb_ShootCE</verbClass>
					<hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
					<defaultProjectile>Projectile_Arrow_Stone</defaultProjectile>
					<warmupTime>1.2</warmupTime>
					<range>40</range>
					<soundCast>Bow_Large</soundCast>
				</li>
			</verbs>
		</value>
	</Operation>

	<Operation Class="SK.PatchOperationReplaceExtended">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Bow_Recurve"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<description>This bow favored by The Horde takes a long time to make but can fire further than a long bow and is also less bulky. It is curved in a manner that allows it to store more energy with a shorter limb. The composite construction is tempermental and difficult to make. Bows require a lot of training to use: An amateur archer may only be effective against targets within 10 or so meters, but a master can hit things 30 or 40m away.</description>
			<graphicData>
				<texPath>Things/Weapons/VileBows/RecurveBow</texPath>
				<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			</graphicData>
			<statBases Merge="True">
				<WorkToMake>7500</WorkToMake>
				<SightsEfficiency>0.95</SightsEfficiency>
				<ShotSpread>0.35</ShotSpread>
				<SwayFactor>2.75</SwayFactor>
				<Mass>1.8</Mass>
				<RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.20</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
			</statBases>
			<verbs>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.VerbPropertiesCE">
					<recoilPattern>Regular</recoilPattern>
					<recoilAmount>1.18</recoilAmount>
					<verbClass>CombatExtended.Verb_ShootCE</verbClass>
					<hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
					<defaultProjectile>Projectile_Arrow_Stone</defaultProjectile>
					<warmupTime>1</warmupTime>
					<range>44</range>
					<soundCast>Bow_Recurve</soundCast>
				</li>
			</verbs>
		</value>
	</Operation>

	<Operation Class="SK.PatchOperationReplaceExtended">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="NorbalBow_Grape"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<label>Jezail Rifled Musket</label>
			<description>Essentially an early sniper rifle, this musket has a rifled barrel to spin the bullet, increasing accuracy. Being muzzle-loaded, that means it's more difficult to load, and the rifling only makes it more difficult. The barrel is exceptionally long which only further increases the range and accuracy. Just don't miss your first shot.</description>
			<graphicData>
				<texPath>Things/Weapons/Jezail</texPath>
				<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			</graphicData>
			<soundInteract>BPInteract</soundInteract>
			<stuffCategories>
				<li>WoodLogs</li>
			</stuffCategories>
			<costStuffCount>75</costStuffCount>
			<costList>
				<ComponentMedieval>5</ComponentMedieval>
			</costList>
			<statBases Merge="True">
				<MarketValue>250</MarketValue>
				<SightsEfficiency>1.05</SightsEfficiency>
				<ShotSpread>0.125</ShotSpread>
				<SwayFactor>2</SwayFactor>
				<RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.8</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
				<Bulk>14</Bulk>
				<Mass>5.8</Mass>
				<WorkToMake>8000</WorkToMake>
				<MaxHitPoints>105</MaxHitPoints>
				<SellPriceFactor>0.3</SellPriceFactor>
			</statBases>
			<weaponTags>
				<!--<li>Gun</li>-->
				<li>Musket</li>
			</weaponTags>
			<thingCategories>
				<li>Rifles</li>
			</thingCategories>
			<verbs>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.VerbPropertiesCE">
					<verbClass>CombatExtended.Verb_ShootCE</verbClass>
					<hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
					<defaultProjectile>Bullet_69Musket_Lead</defaultProjectile>
					<warmupTime>2.8</warmupTime>
					<range>44</range>
					<soundCast>Jezail</soundCast>
					<soundCastTail>GunTail_Heavy</soundCastTail>
					<muzzleFlashScale>12</muzzleFlashScale>
				</li>
			</verbs>
			<comps>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.CompProperties_FireModes">
					<aiAimMode>AimedShot</aiAimMode>
				</li>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.CompProperties_AmmoUser">
					<magazineSize>1</magazineSize>
					<reloadTime>3.5</reloadTime>
					<ammoSet>AmmoSet_69Musket</ammoSet>
				</li>
			</comps>
			<modExtensions>
				<li Class="CombatExtended.GunDrawExtension">
					<DrawSize>1.9,1.9</DrawSize>
				</li>
			</modExtensions>
			<smeltable>True</smeltable>
			<smeltProducts Inherit="false">
				<ComponentMedieval>8</ComponentMedieval>
			</smeltProducts>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>